Z||000015||Fleabitdog||06-14-2001||06:55 PM||||OK, since know one has revealed themselves I won't have to worry about breaking thier anonymity. Bill W ( Wilson) is a cofounder of AA. Some people are very concerned about thier anonymity (That is perfectly understandable) I am a recovering alcoholic(pushing 14 years now)If I would have not sobered up there is no doubt in my mind I would not be alive today. Sorry did not mean to turn this into a testimonial and am not trying to promote anything. I was just curious. Thanks  Dave||||reg||1
Z||000016||WampusCat||06-14-2001||07:02 PM||||Why all the mystery?  He was one of the founders of Alcoholics Anonymous.  This from the official A.A. website:<P>A.A. had its beginnings in 1935 at Akron, Ohio, as the outcome of a meeting between <BR>Bill W., a New York stockbroker, and Dr. Bob S., an Akron surgeon...||||reg||5
